== story
At dawn, a florist wearing a simple linen apron opens Petal & Stem, a small neighbourhood flower shop. The street is still quiet, and warm, natural light touches the doorway as the florist welcomes the new day. Inside, fresh flowers stand in buckets beside a modest worktable. The florist gathers a handful of stems, settles a pale blossom among brighter flowers, and folds paper around the bouquet with practiced care. The arrangement feels personal and freshly made, an everyday gift prepared by someone who knows their craft. A customer in a light jacket arrives at the open door. The florist offers the finished bouquet, and the customer accepts it with a broad, genuine smile. Their brief exchange gives the morning a friendly, neighbourly warmth. The moment ends on the shop front, its Petal & Stem sign readable above the welcoming entrance, with flowers gathered around the doorway in the soft dawn light.
